.TH MITHRIL 1 "2026-09-13" "mithril 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mithril \- analyze firmware contents for secrets, SBOM, CVEs, and licenses
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mithril
.RI [ options ]
.I <file|dir>
.br
.B mithril
.BR \-\-fetch\-db | \-\-update\-db
.RI [ \-\-with\-kernel\-feed ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mithril
reads the contents of firmware and IoT software, a single file or an unpacked
rootfs, and reports four things as structured findings:
.IP \(bu 2
.B secrets:
embedded credential and key material (API tokens, cloud keys, JWTs, private
keys, /etc/shadow hashes), each with a deterministic offline confidence rating.
.IP \(bu 2
.B SBOM:
a software bill of materials built from package databases (dpkg/opkg/apk/rpm),
language manifests, ELF version strings, versioned libc filenames, and the
kernel banner. Emitted as CycloneDX and SPDX.
.IP \(bu 2
.B CVEs:
the SBOM joined against a local offline vulnerability mirror (OSV plus NVD/CPE)
and a curated, version- and kconfig-gated kernel-CVE checklist, annotated with
CISA KEV and EPSS.
.IP \(bu 2
.B licenses:
the open-source licenses present, for compliance and provenance.
.PP
.B mithril
pairs with
.BR moria (1),
which handles structural identification and unpacking. A typical pipeline runs
.B moria \-e
to unpack an image, then
.B mithril
over the extracted tree.
.PP
A scan makes no network calls. The secrets, SBOM, and license passes are fully
offline. The CVE pass reads a local mirror that is refreshed out of band (see
.B THE CVE MIRROR
below), so it is air-gappable once the mirror is in place. Output is
human-readable by default; pass
.BR \-j / \-\-json
for a single JSON object designed to be consumed by a tool or model.
.PP
With no pass flag, every pass runs. Naming one or more passes
.RB ( \-\-secrets ", " \-\-sbom ", " \-\-cve ", " \-\-licenses ", " \-\-boot ", " \-\-keys )
restricts the run to those.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I <file|dir>
A single file, or a directory (typically moria's
.IR .extracted/
output) to scan recursively.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Passes
.TP
.B \-\-secrets
Scan file content for credential and key material.
.TP
.B \-\-sbom
Inventory software components and their versions.
.TP
.B \-\-cve
Match the detected components against known vulnerabilities in the local
mirror. Needs the mirror (see
.BR \-\-fetch\-db ).
.TP
.B \-\-licenses
Identify open-source licenses.
.TP
.B \-\-boot
Boot-security intel: U-Boot environment, device tree, and FIT/AVB/UEFI verified-boot posture.
.TP
.B \-\-keys
Public-key weakness: keys whose private half is public (hardcoded/default keys),
the ROCA fingerprint (CVE-2017-15361), and undersized or broken RSA keys.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-all
Run every pass. This is the default when no pass is named.
.SS Output detail
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Emit a single JSON object instead of the human-readable view. JSON always
carries the complete result set. Use this when a tool or model will parse the
output.
.TP
.B \-\-license\-paths
List the file locations of each license, not just a count (human output).
Implies
.BR \-\-licenses .
.TP
.B \-\-component\-cves\-all
Human view: list every component CVE, not just the high-signal set (on CISA
KEV, or CVSS 9.0 and above, or EPSS 0.10 and above). Implies
.BR \-\-cve .
.TP
.B \-\-kernel\-cves\-all
List every CVE for the detected kernel version, matched branch-aware, instead
of the curated high-signal checklist. Needs the kernel feed (see
.BR \-\-with\-kernel\-feed ).
Implies
.BR \-\-cve .
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-kconfig
Print the recovered kernel
.I .config
to stdout, then exit.
.SS CVE mirror
.TP
.B \-\-fetch\-db
Download a prebuilt CVE mirror and verify it against a published SHA-256, then
exit. Needs
.BR curl .
This is the networked first-run step; see
.B THE CVE MIRROR
below.
.TP
.B \-\-update\-db
Rebuild the local CVE mirror from the upstream feeds, then exit. Slower than
.BR \-\-fetch\-db ;
needs
.B curl
and
.BR unzip .
.TP
.B \-\-with\-kernel\-feed
Given with
.B \-\-fetch\-db
or
.BR \-\-update\-db ,
also fetch the optional full kernel.org (Linux CNA) CVE feed that backs
.BR \-\-kernel\-cves\-all .
.SS Configuration
.TP
.BI \-\-rules " FILE"
Add user-defined detection rules from a JSON file.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-outdir " " \fIDIR\fR
Write the JSON report to
.IR DIR /mithril\-report.json .
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " N"
Worker threads for tree scans. Default: automatic.
.SS Information
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH THE CVE MIRROR
The
.B \-\-cve
pass reads a local mirror under
.B ~/.local/share/mithril
(or
.BR $MITHRIL_DB ),
a compact memory-mapped index built from OSV.dev, the NVD 2.0 API, the CISA KEV
catalog, and FIRST's EPSS scores. On a first run, populate it once with
.B mithril \-\-fetch\-db
before the first CVE scan. Without it,
.B \-\-cve
reports the missing database and exits nonzero. Only
.B \-\-fetch\-db
and
.B \-\-update\-db
ever touch the network; a normal scan does not.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error (for example, an unreadable target or a missing CVE mirror for
.BR \-\-cve ).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown option, missing argument).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MITHRIL_DB
Path to the local CVE mirror (overrides the default under
.BR ~/.local/share/mithril ).
.TP
.B MITHRIL_DB_URL
Base URL that
.B \-\-fetch\-db
downloads the prebuilt mirror from.
.TP
.B NVD_API_KEY
Optional NVD API key used by
.B \-\-update\-db
to raise the upstream rate limit. It works without one, just more slowly.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
If set,
.B mithril
locates the mirror under
.B $XDG_DATA_HOME/mithril
instead of
.BR ~/.local/share/mithril .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables bold section headers in
.B \-\-help
output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/mithril/
Default location of the local CVE mirror (OSV plus NVD/CPE index, KEV, EPSS, and
the optional kernel feed).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run every analysis on an unpacked tree:
.B mithril ./rootfs/
.TP
Only the secrets pass:
.B mithril \-\-secrets ./rootfs/
.TP
JSON output for a tool or model:
.B mithril \-j ./rootfs/
.TP
First run: download the CVE mirror:
.B mithril \-\-fetch\-db
.TP
The full pipeline with moria:
.B moria \-e firmware.bin && mithril firmware.bin.extracted/
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR moria (1),
.BR trufflehog (1)
.PP
Full documentation: README.md and docs/ in the source tree
.RB ( https://github.com/nmatt0/mithril ).
